Corrects f-s3-skill-r1-11, which left the C and C++ examples in section B under-sourced. The section's sources sentence gains:
- the `fgets` behaviour: keeps the newline, returns a null pointer on failure;
- the `sizeof`-of-a-pointer caveat;
- `make_unique` since C++14;
- C++ Core Guidelines R.23 and R.11, read on a mirror because the canonical page was cut off; the report advises re-reading R.23 on isocpp.github.io before relying on it;
- CWE-477 for the category as a whole.

